      "writtenOn": "2022-11-23T22:37:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We would like bindings to be reproducible (so they can be regenerated as needed for  bindgen/Rust updates or header changes), either by:\n\n1 - Writing a `bindgen.sh` script like the other ones in the crosvm tree to regenerate the bindings automatically from a fixed version of the Linux kernel source tree.\n\nor\n\n2 - Adding the bindgen command plus any other necessary instructions (e.g. how to get the right version of the headers) to a comment header in the generated file.\n\n(Option 1 is preferred, but it\u0027s OK to do it manually for now if the headers are not available in the kernel yet.)\n\nIdeally this should also be filtered down to the relevant definitions using bindgen\u0027s `--allowlist-type`, `--allowlist-function`, etc. with regexes that just match the Gunyah declarations (for example, `__BITS_PER_LONG`, `__kernel_uid32_t`, etc. are not relevant and don\u0027t need to be in the bindings). You can also set `--no-layout-tests` to cut down on a lot of the cruft.",
      "revId": "676e61483f6d76128e25d74c63d9e87b3a779150",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
